{
    "background_story": "Vance was a meticulous and organized individual who believed in planning for every eventuality. As a successful event planner, he had a reputation for attention to detail and precision timing. But little did anyone know that Vance's penchant for prearrangement extended far beyond his professional life. He had a secret: he had planned out his entire life, from the smallest details to the biggest milestones. From the age of 20, Vance had a binder filled with timelines, spreadsheets, and contingency plans for every possible scenario. His friends and family often joked that he had his funeral planned out, and they weren't far off. Vance's prearrangement obsession was both a source of comfort and a coping mechanism for the unpredictability of life. While some might find it eccentric, Vance saw it as a way to ensure that every moment counted.",
